perturbations.a:
OctoberCMS 401, 402, 403, 503, 400 error code management

I just need to inquire is octobercms has only adept at configuring two types of errors ???

  1. 404 [by establishing a page with /404 url ]

  2. 500 [by establishing a page with /error url ]

how can we configure 400, 401, 402, 403, 503, 400 etc ??????

Those 2 are exceptional cases where author already created code in Cms Main Controller but for others we need to develop code on our own :)

Hmm all are connected to HttpException so these are the codes indeed we configure and raise like this,

App::abort(403, 'Access is prohibited to the requested page.' /* message */);

Now these all are HttpException, We can intercept them utilizing App::error. You need to insert this code into your plugin boot method.

//\App::error(function(\Exception $exception) { // for managing all Exceptions

// for managing http related exceptions
\App::error(function(
    \Symfony\Component\HttpKernel\Exception\HttpException $exception) {

    dd($exception->getStatusCode()); /* 403 */ // 400, 401, 402, 403, 503, 400 etc            
    // Handle the exception...
});

You can verify status-code here and manage them as you prefer. Reference: https://octobercms.com/docs/services/error-log#http-exceptions

