perturbations.a:
Transform int to string/char C++/Arduino

This has got to be the simplest thing to accomplish in C++.

..and I recognize it's been posed many many times previously, however please keep in consideration that this is part of an Arduino project and memory conservation is a significant concern as I've only got 32256 byte utmost to play with.

I need to transform an integer to a string.

int GSM_BAUD_RATE;
GSM_BAUD_RATE = 4800;

Serial.println("GSM Shield operating at " + GSM_BAUD_RATE + " baud rate.");

Evidently the last line is going to provide me an error.

Thanks in advance.


If, as it appears, you are engaged in an Arduino project, you should simply allow the Serial object manage it:

int GSM_BAUD_RATE;
GSM_BAUD_RATE = 4800;

Serial.print("GSM Shield operating at ");
Serial.print(GSM_BAUD_RATE);
Serial.println(" baud rate.");

since the print and println functions have overloads to manage various different types.

The other functions can be beneficial on "normal" machines, but items like string and ostringstream necessitate heap allocation, which, on an Arduino board, should be evaded if feasible due to the strict memory limitations.

